       <h1>Akhilesh Yadav Accuses Yogi Adityanath of Insulting Lord Krishna</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Samajwadi Party leader Akhilesh Yadav has accused Uttar Pradesh Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath of insulting Lord Krishna and cowherds following remarks Adityanath made in Uttarakhand. Yadav claimed the Chief Minister’s language regarding his background was offensive and vowed the BJP would face defeat in the 2027 assembly elections.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/akhilesh-yadav-accuses-yogi-adityanath-of-insulting-lord-kri.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Yadav further criticized Adityanath for allegedly disrespecting the Pal community and the statue of Rajmata Devi Ahilyabai Holkar. He characterized the Chief Minister’s recent rhetoric as a sign of political weakness and frustration, predicting a permanent electoral loss for the BJP in the upcoming polls.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the political accusations and the context of the 2027 election, maintaining a neutral tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/uttar-pradesh/story/akhilesh-yadav-accuses-yogi-adityanath-lord-krishna-insult-bjp-defeat-2027-ptag-3037221-2026-11-12?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
