     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Carlos Alcaraz Drawn With Daniil Medvedev, Alexander Zverev To Face Ben Shelton At ATP Finals</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Tennis</span> <span>#ATP Finals</span> <span>#Carlos Alcaraz</span> <span>#Alexander Zverev</span></div>
       <p>World No. 1 Alexander Zverev and second seed Carlos Alcaraz have learned their group-stage opponents for the 2026 ATP Finals, following the draw announcement made in Turin on Thursday. Two-time champion Zverev has been placed in the John McEnroe Group, where he will compete against American Ben Shelton, France's Arthur Fils, and Spain's Rafael Jodar. Alcaraz, the second seed, will headline the Ivan Lendl Group, which features Russia's Daniil Medvedev, Italy's Flavio Cobolli, and American Frances Tiafoe. The season-ending tournament is scheduled to be held at the Inalpi Arena from November 15 to 22, with players competing across two groups for a spot in the semifinals.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/carlos-alcaraz-drawn-with-daniil-medvedev-alexander-zverev-t.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Zverev, who previously secured the ATP Finals title in both 2018 and 2021, will be aiming to add a third trophy to his collection. Alcaraz, making his fourth appearance at the tournament and having reached the final last year, will be looking to win this prestigious season-ending title for the first time. The 23-year-old Spaniard heads into the competition in impressive form, having won titles in Paris, Vienna, and Tokyo following his return from injury at the US Open.</p><p>Former champion Daniil Medvedev, who won the title in 2020, is expected to be among Alcaraz's main challengers within the Ivan Lendl Group. Flavio Cobolli will lead Italy's challenge at the home tournament, particularly in the absence of Jannik Sinner, who has withdrawn due to injury. Ben Shelton will be making his second appearance at the season-ending event, while Arthur Fils, Frances Tiafoe, Flavio Cobolli, and Rafael Jodar are all set to make their debuts.</p><p>The doubles draw was also announced on Thursday. Defending champions Harri Heliovaara and Henry Patten will lead the Todd Woodbridge Group. ATP Finals action is set to commence on Sunday at the Inalpi Arena. The eight-man field will be reduced to four for the semifinals, scheduled for Saturday, November 21, with the final to be held on Sunday, November 22.</p><p>What to watch: The ATP Finals begin Sunday at the Inalpi Arena.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source information regarding the ATP Finals draw and player details. It efficiently summarizes the event schedule and player backgrounds.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/tennis/carlos-alcaraz-drawn-with-daniil-medvedev-alexander-zverev-to-face-ben-shelton-at-atp-finals-12319254#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
