     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Fujairah Truck Crash Kills 14, Injures 30; Indians Among Deceased</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#UAE</span> <span>#Fujairah</span> <span>#Road Accident</span> <span>#Indian Nationals</span></div>
       <p>A major road accident in the United Arab Emirates’ Fujairah emirate resulted in the deaths of 14 people and left 30 injured, according to News18 World. The incident, described by Reuters as one of the UAE’s deadliest road crashes, occurred shortly before midnight on Sheikh Khalifa bin Zayed Road, near the entrance to Fujairah. The collision involved a truck losing control, overturning, and crashing into several vehicles, triggering a massive fire.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/fujairah-truck-crash-kills-14-injures-30-indians-among-decea.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Fujairah Police, cited by Reuters, stated that the truck driver lost control of the vehicle while traveling on Sheikh Khalifa bin Zayed Road. The truck first collided with another vehicle before overturning and striking a number of vehicles that were stopped because of slow-moving traffic on the street. The UAE interior ministry, in a statement quoted by AFP, added that the impact caused the truck to catch fire, with the blaze quickly spreading to several other vehicles involved, causing a &quot;heavy loss of life.&quot;</p><p>The Indian Consulate in Dubai confirmed that Indian nationals were among those killed in the accident. The consulate stated it was coordinating with local authorities to provide assistance and support to the bereaved families, according to an online statement posted by the consulate, AFP reported. Fujairah Police further confirmed that Emirati nationals were also among the deceased. Authorities initiated DNA testing to establish the identities of some of those killed, Reuters noted, as efforts are underway to identify other victims through DNA analysis. The exact number of Indian nationals killed was not specified.</p><p>Authorities confirmed on Thursday that 14 lives were lost and 30 people injured. Of those injured, 15 had been discharged from hospital, while the remaining 15 continued to receive medical treatment, according to Fujairah Police via Reuters. Emergency response teams, including police personnel, ambulance crews, and civil defence units, rushed to the accident site to extinguish the fire, evacuate the injured to nearby hospitals, and secure the area.</p><p>What to watch: Continued efforts for victim identification and support for affected families.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive coverage of the incident, including casualty figures, police statements, and the involvement of the Indian Consulate.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/indians-among-14-killed-as-truck-crashes-into-multiple-vehicles-catches-fire-in-uaes-fujairah-10423725.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-11-12/fujairah-truck-crash-kills-14-injures-30-indians-among-decea" data-title="Fujairah Truck Crash Kills 14, Injures 30; Indians Among Deceased"><b>Share:</b>
