       <h1>IAF adopts indigenous AI as Rajnath Singh calls for future-ready warfare</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#IAF</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Air Force (IAF) has adopted indigenous artificial intelligence (AI) solutions, marking a significant step in modernizing its operational capabilities. This development aligns with calls for enhanced future-ready warfare strategies, as reported by The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/iaf-adopts-indigenous-ai-as-rajnath-singh-calls-for-future-r.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Defence Minister Rajnath Singh has emphasized the necessity for the armed forces to be prepared for future conflicts, advocating for the integration of advanced technologies. The IAF's move to incorporate domestically developed AI systems reflects this strategic imperative, aiming to bolster its technological edge.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on the specific AI applications adopted by the IAF.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and accurately reflects the provided summary.</p>
