       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-12 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>IAF Opens AFCAT 01/2027 Application for Flying, Ground Duty Posts</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Careers</span> <span>#IAF</span> <span>#AFCAT</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Air Force (IAF) has commenced the application window for AFCAT 01/2027, as reported by The Times of India. This registration process is open for candidates seeking to join the Flying and Ground Duty branches of the IAF.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/iaf-opens-afcat-012027-application-for-flying-ground-duty-po.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Prospective applicants can now register for the examination, which serves as a gateway to various roles within the Air Force. The official announcement indicates that the application window opened &quot;today.&quot;</p><p>What to watch: Monitor the official IAF website for application details.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source summary. It is concise and does not invent details, though it is quite short due to the limited source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
