       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>IMD Forecasts Light Showers in Andhra Pradesh; Low-Pressure System Developing</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The India Meteorological Department (IMD) predicts isolated light showers across Andhra Pradesh on November 13 and 14, followed by dry weather until November 19. A low-pressure area is expected to form over the southeast Bay of Bengal on Friday, potentially intensifying into a depression by November 15.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/imd-forecasts-light-showers-in-andhra-pradesh-low-pressure-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Squally winds reaching up to 65 kmph are forecasted for the central and southern Bay of Bengal between November 14 and 17. Despite the system's potential intensification beyond a depression, experts indicate the state is unlikely to face a direct impact, as the projected landfall is not expected to strike the eastern coast.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Highly dense and accurate reporting of the meteorological forecast and the specific timeline provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/light-showers-likely-on-nov-13-and-14-in-ap/article71694405.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
