     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>John Kerry Criticizes Trump on Climate Action at Cop31</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Climate Change</span> <span>#Politics</span> <span>#Environment</span></div>
       <p>Former US Secretary of State John Kerry has strongly criticized Donald Trump at the Cop31 climate summit in Turkey, labeling him the “biggest loser we’ve seen in a long time” for his approach to the climate crisis. Kerry asserted that Trump's actions led to the United States ceding clean-energy dominance to China and emphasized that the climate crisis remains a key issue for voters.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/john-kerry-criticizes-trump-on-climate-action-at-cop31.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Speaking from the resort city of Antalya, Kerry specifically highlighted Trump's decision to withdraw the US from the international climate process. He also pointed to the previous administration's dismantling of measures designed to reduce planet-heating emissions, which Kerry views as detrimental to global climate efforts.</p><p>A notable absence at the annual UN climate talks, which commenced on Monday, is a delegation from the Trump administration. Unlike nearly all other participating countries, the former president's team has not sent representatives to the summit in Turkey.</p><p>What to watch: The ongoing discussions and commitments at the Cop31 climate summit.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures all major elements of John Kerry's statements, Cop31 context, and Trump's absence.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/12/trump-loser-john-kerry-cop31" rel="noopener">Guardian Environment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
