     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kurnool Officials Ban Irrigation Use of Drinking Water Reserves</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Kurnool District Collector A. Siri has ordered that water in the Gajuladinne and Sunkesula projects be reserved exclusively for drinking, prohibiting its use for Rabi season crop irrigation. With insufficient rainfall threatening local supply, officials are forming teams to educate farmers on these restrictions to ensure adequate reserves through next June.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/kurnool-officials-ban-irrigation-use-of-drinking-water-reser.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Separately, KMC Commissioner Challa Obulesu warned that illegal water diversion from the K-C Canal will result in motor seizures and legal action. Authorities are also accelerating the construction of an ₹82 crore pipeline between Sunkesula and the Munagalapadu summer storage tank to secure the city’s water supply against potential shortages.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Efficiently condenses the directives regarding water management and the specific infrastructure project mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
