     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-11-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Marshall Islands President Warns Climate Crisis Threatens Island Existence at COP31</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#COP31</span> <span>#Marshall Islands</span> <span>#Climate Change</span> <span>#Floods</span></div>
       <p>During a passionate address at COP31 in Turkey on Wednesday, Marshall Islands President Hilda Heine warned that without an overwhelming response to the climate crisis, “the world we know is over.” Heine, one of the few Pacific Island leaders speaking at the summit, highlighted that overshooting the 1.5 °C Paris target would cause sea‑level rise that erodes shorelines and triggers floods capable of destroying towns, schools and hospitals across low‑lying nations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/marshall-islands-president-warns-climate-crisis-threatens-is.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Heine’s remarks underscored the immediate danger faced by her island nation, which has already experienced worsening floods. The president’s plea echoed broader calls from UN chief António Guterres, who urged a windfall tax on oil and gas firms to fund climate mitigation and adaptation. Heine emphasized that the stakes are existential for the Marshall Islands, where even modest temperature increases translate into existential threats to habitability.</p><p>The speech came as dozens of world leaders gathered in Turkey, debating financing mechanisms and emission‑reduction pathways. While Heine’s warning resonated with other vulnerable states, the summit’s outcomes remain uncertain, with negotiations over the proposed windfall tax still ongoing. What to watch: progress on the windfall tax proposal and any concrete commitments to support Pacific island nations vulnerable to rising seas.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive and accurate summary of the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/11/the-world-we-know-is-over-marshall-islands-president-cop31" rel="noopener">Guardian Environment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
