     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mitchell Marsh confirms Australia's top six for England ODI series, eyeing 2027 World Cup</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Australia</span> <span>#ODI</span> <span>#England</span></div>
       <p>Australia's stand-in captain Mitchell Marsh announced the batting order for the upcoming ODI series against England, confirming the same combination will feature in Perth on Friday, November 13. Marsh believes this top six represents the nation's best chance at the 2027 ODI World Cup, scheduled for South Africa, Zimbabwe, and Namibia.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/mitchell-marsh-confirms-australias-top-six-for-england-odi-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The announced top six includes Marsh himself, Travis Head, Cooper Connolly, Matt Renshaw, Josh Inglis, and Cameron Green. This line-up will take the field in the opening match of the three-game series, which runs through November 18 across Perth, Adelaide, and Hobart. Marsh was quoted by Cricinfo stating, &quot;We've got a batting line-up that I see being at that World Cup, and it's sort of where we end up.&quot;</p><p>This selection marks a significant shift from recent ODI teams. Steven Smith has stepped away from the format, while Marnus Labuschagne has not featured since July, having struggled with form and been dropped from the Test side, despite being part of Australia's 2023 World Cup-winning squad. Additionally, Pat Cummins, Josh Hazlewood, and Mitchell Starc are unavailable for the series as they prepare for the Test schedule.</p><p>Opening the door for new talent, Western Australian fast bowler Mahli Beardman is set to make his international debut in the first ODI. Beardman previously appeared in one T20 International in Pakistan earlier this year. Marsh expressed strong confidence in the young prospect, stating, &quot;He's an amazing talent. He's a ripping young kid... He loves to bowl fast, and that's an attitude that you can't always teach.&quot;</p><p>What to watch: The performance of the new batting order and Mahli Beardman's debut.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively integrates all key personnel, the upcoming series schedule, and the context regarding player availability and selection.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/mitchell-marsh-spills-the-beans-on-australias-potential-top-six-for-2027-odi-world-cup/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
