       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>New Blood Test Detects Early Ovarian Cancer Risk</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ovarian Cancer</span> <span>#Blood Test</span> <span>#Nature Medicine</span></div>
       <p>Researchers published a report in Nature Medicine on Tuesday describing a blood test that can identify an early risk of ovarian cancer. The study marks a shift from previous efforts that focused on finding smaller tumours, aiming instead to flag the disease before it develops fully. By analysing specific biomarkers in the bloodstream, the test offers a potential tool for earlier intervention, though the summary does not disclose the test’s sensitivity, specificity, or the size of the study cohort. What to watch: adoption of the test in clinical screening programs.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/new-blood-test-detects-early-ovarian-cancer-risk.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
