       <h1>Palantir CEO Alex Karp Claims Progressive Identity Amid Past Controversies</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Palantir CEO Alex Karp recently told Politico that he considers himself a lifelong Democrat and views his company's products as fundamentally progressive. This pivot follows recent election results that analysts describe as a difficult period for right-leaning founders.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/palantir-ceo-alex-karp-claims-progressive-identity-amid-past.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Karp's assertion contrasts with his documented history, including his 2025 declaration that Palantir is &quot;completely anti-woke&quot; and his previous statements advocating for &quot;organized violence&quot; and the lethality of military data analysis. Karp has also frequently criticized elite institutions and Democratic party factions while maintaining his company's focus on national defense and special operations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the CEO's recent comments and historical contradictions provided in the text.</p>
