     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-11-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>PM Modi Cites World Bank Data on India's Poverty Reduction</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Prime Minister Narendra Modi addressed journalists at a Diwali Milan event, contrasting the historical 'Garibi Hatao' slogan with recent World Bank data. The report indicates that approximately 49.6 crore people in India rose above the lower-middle-income poverty threshold between 2011 and 2023, while extreme poverty rates declined from 27.1% to 2.6%.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/pm-modi-cites-world-bank-data-on-indias-poverty-reduction.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Modi also reflected on the evolution of media technology, noting that mobile phones have replaced traditional outside broadcast vans. He urged journalists to increase coverage of India’s success stories and requested that the media help raise public awareness regarding the ongoing fight against drug abuse.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief correctly identifies the PM's remarks and the specific World Bank data cited in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/pm-modi-contrasts-garibi-hatao-slogan-with-indias-poverty-reduction-cites-world-bank-at-diwali-milan-10422770.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
