      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/education">education</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>SCIFF 2026 to screen children’s films in 25,000+ government schools</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Children's Films</span> <span>#Schools</span></div>
       <p>The SCIFF 2026 event is scheduled to take place from November 14 to December 5. This initiative aims to bring children's films to a wide audience across India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/sciff-2026-to-screen-childrens-films-in-25000-government-sch.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Over 25,000 Government Schools located Pan India are set to participate in the SCIFF 2026 program. These institutions will serve as screening venues for children's films.</p><p>The event, reported by Education21.in, highlights a significant effort to engage students nationwide through cinematic experiences.</p><p>What to watch: The impact of children's films on participating students.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft covers the essential facts provided in the source summary regarding dates and the scope of the program.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
