     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-11-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sensex and Nifty See Marginal Gains Amid Sectoral Swings on November 12, 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Stock Market</span> <span>#Sensex</span> <span>#Nifty</span> <span>#Market Updates</span></div>
       <p>India's benchmark indices, the Sensex and Nifty50, experienced marginal gains on Thursday, November 12, 2026, as trading remained narrow and fluctuated between profit and loss. As of 12:00 PM, the Sensex climbed 89.74 points, or 0.11 per cent, to reach 81,969.14. Concurrently, the Nifty50 advanced by 14.55 points, a 0.06 per cent increase, settling at 25,269.60, according to Business Standard.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/sensex-and-nifty-see-marginal-gains-amid-sectoral-swings-on-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In sectoral performance, IT, FMCG, and auto shares emerged as the primary drags on the market. Conversely, Nifty Realty demonstrated outperformance. Within the Nifty50, Bajaj Finance, Shriram Finance, and Bajaj Finserv were identified as the top gainers, contributing positively to the index's movement.</p><p>Broader markets also registered gains, with the Nifty MidCap index rising by 0.11 per cent. The Nifty SmallCap index showed a stronger performance, increasing by 0.72 per cent. These movements indicate a mixed sentiment across different segments of the Indian equity market on the trading day.</p><p>A significant number of companies were scheduled to release their Q2 results on Wednesday, November 11, 2026. These included Action Construction Equipment, Alkem Laboratories, Amber Enterprises India, Astra Microwave Products, Automotive Axles, Avalon Technologies, Bharat Dynamics, Bondada Engineering, Caplin Point Laboratories, Dilip Buildcon, Dollar Industries, EIH, Elevate Campuses, EMS, Ethos, Fiem Industries, Hindustan Aeronautics, Hinduja Global Solutions, Vodafone Idea, IFCI, Indian Railway Catering &amp; Tourism Corporation (IRCTC), Kennametal India, Kesoram Industries, Landmark Cars, Manappuram Finance, Man Industries (India), NMDC, NMDC Steel, Oil India, Ola Electric Mobility, Oswal Pumps, Page Industries, Procter &amp; Gamble Hygiene &amp; Health Care, Hitachi Energy India, Premier Explosives, Rane Holdings, Rashtriya Chemicals &amp; Fertilizers (RCF), Religare Enterprises, Reliance Power, Sharda Motor Industries, S.P. Apparels, TARC, Tarsons Products, TD Power Systems, Techno Electric &amp; Engineering Company, Travel Food Services, and Uflex.</p><p>What to watch: Monitor the impact of Q2 results on individual stock movements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Excellent synthesis of the provided source text, capturing market performance, sectoral trends, and the extensive list of companies releasing results.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/stock-market-live-november-12-gift-nifty-nse-bse-sensex-today-nifty50-crude-oil-prices-q2-results-today-126111200066_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
