     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Seven Bangladesh Players Register for IPL 2027 Auction, Mustafizur Rahman Included</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#IPL</span> <span>#Bangladesh</span> <span>#Auction</span></div>
       <p>Seven Bangladeshi cricketers, including prominent fast bowler Mustafizur Rahman, have registered for the Indian Premier League (IPL) 2027 mini-auction, scheduled for December 16 in Goa. The contingent features five fast bowlers: Mustafizur Rahman, Nahid Rana, Hasan Mahmud, Taskin Ahmed, and Shoriful Islam. They are joined by all-rounder Rishad Hossain and batter Towhid Hridoy, who is the sole specialist batter among the registered players.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/seven-bangladesh-players-register-for-ipl-2027-auction-musta.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Mustafizur Rahman's registration is a notable development, particularly after his release from Kolkata Knight Riders (KKR) in 2026. KKR had acquired him for Rs 9.20 crore before being directed to release him weeks later. The Bangladesh Cricket Board (BCB) confirmed these registrations through its cricket operations in-charge, Shahriar Nafees Ahmed, who stated that eight players had completed their registration by the November 23 cut-off date, with others still considering. Nafees clarified that this is a &quot;regular procedure for the IPL auction&quot; and that the BCCI had sent a link inviting players to register.</p><p>The 2026 season was marked by significant tension between Indian and Bangladesh cricket authorities. KKR's release of Mustafizur followed a directive from the Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI), which emerged amid escalating political tensions between the two nations. This was further strained by Bangladesh's withdrawal from the T20 World Cup earlier that year, impacting bilateral relations between the boards.</p><p>Despite these past tensions, Shahriar Nafees Ahmed indicated an improvement in relations. He was quoted by Sportstar saying, &quot;The relationship between the two boards has always been very good and cordial, and we have always maintained that. Yes, there was a hiccup last year, but that’s all in the past now. We now share a very good relationship with the BCCI and both the boards want to play good cricket and develop more talents.&quot;</p><p>However, franchise interest in Bangladeshi players remains uncertain, with several IPL teams signalling a preference to await formal clarity from the BCCI before committing to recruitment decisions. This cautious approach reflects lingering uncertainty from last year's political situation and the absence of explicit assurance from Indian cricket authorities regarding player participation. Discussions between BCCI officials and Bangladesh Cricket Board president Tamim Iqbal, who is currently attending an ICC meeting in Bali, could provide the clarity franchises seek, potentially determining player signings for the 2027 season.</p><p>What to watch: The outcome of discussions between BCCI and BCB officials regarding player participation for the 2027 IPL season.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Thoroughly mirrors the source, covering player list, registration details, quotes, and contextual tensions without adding unsupported information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/mustafizur-rahman-nahid-rana-among-seven-bangladesh-players-registered-for-ipl-2027-auction-2260/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
