     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-12 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tamil Nadu Minister Rejects Karnataka’s Mekedatu Dam Plans</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Tamil Nadu Water Resources Minister N. Anand stated that Karnataka will be unable to construct a dam across the Cauvery River at Mekedatu, despite recent claims by Karnataka Chief Minister D.K. Shivakumar. Mr. Anand met with Union Minister for Jal Shakti C.R. Patil to discuss ongoing water projects, including the Jal Jeevan Mission, while confirming state-sanctioned rehabilitation for Mukkombu’s damaged barrage.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/tamil-nadu-minister-rejects-karnatakas-mekedatu-dam-plans.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During his visit to the Upper Anicut, Mr. Anand reviewed maintenance operations for the barrages. The state has allocated ₹126 crore to repair the protective apron and structure, which sustained severe erosion during heavy floods in 2021 and 2022. Rehabilitation work is scheduled to commence shortly.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the meeting and the minister's statement on the Mekedatu dam while incorporating the correct financial figure.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/karnataka-can-never-build-a-dam-at-mekedatu-says-minister/article71694034.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-11-12/tamil-nadu-minister-rejects-karnatakas-mekedatu-dam-plans" data-title="Tamil Nadu Minister Rejects Karnataka’s Mekedatu Dam Plans"><b>Share:</b>
