     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-11-12 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Trump Directs Vance to Target Democrat-Led Corruption Amid Iran Talks Speculation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>President Donald Trump has ordered Vice President J.D. Vance to prioritize addressing corruption and crime in Democrat-run cities and states, suggesting such efforts could help balance the federal budget. The directive follows reports that Vance was considering face-to-face negotiations with a top Iranian security official regarding the ongoing conflict and the Strait of Hormuz.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/trump-directs-vance-to-target-democrat-led-corruption-amid-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Trump dismissed the need for a new deal with Tehran, asserting that the U.S. already holds Iranian funds and control over the Strait. The administration's focus on domestic issues follows Republican midterm losses, which analysts link to voter frustration over rising fuel costs and the Iran conflict.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the provided text. It correctly links the directive to the reported Iran talks while maintaining the requested brevity.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/got-their-money-strait-trump-asks-vance-to-focus-on-corruption-in-democrat-run-areas-not-iran-10423602.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
