     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-11-12 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Trump Suggests Tim Cook for Nvidia CEO After Jensen Huang's Resignation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Business</span> <span>#Technology</span> <span>#Nvidia</span> <span>#Apple</span></div>
       <p>US President Donald Trump publicly suggested on Thursday that former Apple Inc. Chief Executive Tim Cook should take over as CEO of Nvidia, following the resignation of Jensen Huang. Trump stated on social media, &quot;NOW THAT Nvidia CEO JENSEN HUANG, who has done a fantastic job, has resigned, there is only one man to take his place - TIM COOK of Apple.&quot; He further added, &quot;A Legend replaces a Legend!&quot; The proposal comes after Huang stepped down from his role as CEO and a member of the board on the same day.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-12/trump-suggests-tim-cook-for-nvidia-ceo-after-jensen-huangs-r.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Huang's resignation on Thursday was prompted by reports alleging an affair with a Chinese businesswoman, whom US authorities suspect of spying for Beijing. In response, Nvidia has named Chief Financial Officer Colette Kress as the interim CEO. President Trump, who maintains close ties with top US tech executives, revealed on Monday that he had discussed the matter with Huang. According to Trump, Huang claimed he was unaware that the woman linked to him was allegedly a spy.</p><p>Tim Cook, who served as Apple's CEO for 15 years, stepped down from that position in September and currently holds the title of executive chairman at the iPhone-maker. Apple and Cook did not immediately respond to requests for comment regarding Trump's suggestion. Cook has previously engaged with the Trump administration; last year, he presented Trump with a custom US-made plaque commemorating Apple's &quot;American Manufacturing Program&quot; after the company pledged an additional $100 billion investment in domestic manufacturing.</p><p>Jensen Huang has been identified as one of Trump's closest allies in Silicon Valley, with their relationship reportedly dating back to at least 2025. Over the past two years, Huang has consistently voiced support for the administration's agenda and frequently appeared in Washington, particularly as Nvidia pursued opportunities to sell advanced chips in the Chinese market.</p><p>What to watch: Nvidia's leadership transition and its future strategic direction.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the full text, maintaining all key details, quotes, and chronological events without adding external invention.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/iran-deal-not-needed-trump-asks-vance-to-focus-on-domestic-corruption-126111201547_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
